    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-040",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3125827-040",
      "text": "A malicious party using Sybil accounts cannot be prevented from cloning the structure of a successful proof of stake blockchain at far lower cost than cloning a proof of work chain, leaving a new user unable to distinguish the truly decentralized chain from a clone that has manufactured even more tokens. The authors answer that this is resolved off chain, by a trusted user interface, as with cloned web pages.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "blockchain",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "new users joining without prior knowledge of the genuine chain",
        "PoS chains where clone creation costs only new public keys"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3125827-040:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Then, when a new user joins the network, how will they be able to distinguish a truly decentralized blockchain from a cloned blockchain that has manufactured an even larger number of tokens?",
      "text_sha256": "a1a15342ca61c3d998515944b9d1aa7f8904b39e5637a12c4a5ff22e7e0f9efa",
      "source_sha256": "598d9bd95e4af7a0a35328677c6bfc069f69f2e32c30c720b3a0be98a23a40cb",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-015",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-015",
      "text": "Semada is stipulated as an autonomous, decentralized, open source protocol on the Ethereum blockchain that enables domain specific reputation verification for human task crowdsourcing.",
      "claim_type": "definitional",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-015:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Semada is an autonomous, decentralized, open-source protocol29 that enables domain specific reputation verification for human task crowdsourcing, built on the ETHEREUM blockchain.",
      "text_sha256": "f69e861e95d9441ee2e602cb46f4b3d1c7bccb53bbf76de8b2720aa5f771031d",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-016",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-016",
      "text": "The protocol lowers cost because it removes the manual verification step and the associated multiplication of micro task work that centralized systems require, letting decentralized workers capture the gains from disintermediation.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "decentralization",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "micro task crowdsourcing under the Semada Protocol"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-016:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "the Semada Protocol removes the manual verification and the associated multiplication of micro task work necessitated by centralized systems, enabling its decentralized micro task workers to profit from the disintermediation.",
      "text_sha256": "f1e1d2f5e6db14dfb3f4e63a2c5d308d3c42b6a1c35c246caceda4ace6ac7f2a",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-017",
      "text": "Reputation tokens supply a staking mechanism that incentivizes high quality work and task completion by workers, and that simultaneously lets requesters verify and track worker quality, integrity, and quantity.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "tokenomics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "participants staking reputation tokens on the platform"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 87
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Through the reputation tokens, the Semada Protocol provides a micro task worker reputation staking mechanism that incentivizes high quality work and task completion by workers.",
      "text_sha256": "0a521ab5ff37dee60b817f13e4f5d96e865ac6ab67e4f121da9f1a05077b267e",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-018",
      "text": "Unlike its decentralized competitors, the Semada Protocol is claimed to be resistant to both Sybil attacks and Tyranny of the Majority attacks.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "comparison with existing decentralized mechanical turk protocols"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 65
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-018:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, unlike its decentralized competitors, the Semada Protocol ensures Sybil Attack and Tyranny of the Majority attack resistance.",
      "text_sha256": "391ca1a76812d268a01e502239bf1ebb63ef1a2aabae4861df03a360ac5f7b41",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-019",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-019",
      "text": "The protocol architecture together with its incentive structure is what produces enhanced 51 percent attack resistance, which the author claims exceeds prior reputation verification attempts in both decentralized and centralized networks.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives",
        "reputation",
        "blockchain"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "reputation verification networks"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "asserted",
      "relevance_score": 77
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-019:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The Semada Protocol architecture and its incentive structure facilitates enhanced 51% attack resistance unlike any previous reputation verification attempts in decentralized and centralized networks.",
      "text_sha256": "e65b5d5d5057493881d76c85dc8496dd1b3c41e21ccb948cf292f3b1544bed91",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-023",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-023",
      "text": "Rather than repeating the same task across many workers to reach quality, the architecture verifies quality directly by examining and validating individual worker task performance through reputation verification.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "micro tasks routed through the reputation verification architecture"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 70
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-023:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Instead of repeating work on given tasks to attain high quality work products for micro tasks, Semada uses an architecture of reputation verification that examines micro worker task performance and verifies the validity and quality of the work.",
      "text_sha256": "ba5551661e84ce2ff26b44e3f2a905314d17adff366e7981244ec968a639c471",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-024",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-024",
      "text": "Staking creates disincentives for malicious actors, and it is this disincentive structure that makes the network both more efficient and attack resistant.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "workers and verifiers who have reputation tokens at stake"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 74
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-024:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Semada staking mechanism creates disincentives for malicious actors, enhancing the efficiency of the Semada Network and making it attack resistant.",
      "text_sha256": "5258c7e8874d16e25e758c2b51d4f2f843ab85400d905514a6ab80b1e187a471",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-037",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-037",
      "text": "Attack resistance should be designed to increase as the platform grows, in contrast to designs like GEMS that detect and ban malicious actors, because a self enforcement mechanism lets the incentive system steer users away from bad actors once the system matures.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "compliance",
        "consensus-and-security",
        "governance-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "after the system reaches maturity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 74
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-037:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Unlike GEMS, which bans malicious actors detected through the GEMS trust mechanism from the platform, the Semada platform has a self-enforcement mechanism.",
      "text_sha256": "6b07adc051822d27c518e6669a51b73774928679d00421ddc3cb9df91cc599fa",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-045",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-045",
      "text": "Centralized platforms cannot simply drop identity verification, because they need it to keep malicious actors from abusing the network and to ensure work quality; this is the tradeoff a staking based design is meant to dissolve.",
      "claim_type": "condition",
      "topics": [
        "institutional-design"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "centralized micro task platforms"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 64
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-045:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "However, centralized micro task platforms need to verify identity to prevent malicious actors from abusing the network and ensure work quality.",
      "text_sha256": "2a43089b86d9a883388b8cbb71b6ca488dd4743152b11fa8ce591dcf01fa0675",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-046",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3128900-046",
      "text": "Because the reputation token staking mechanism supplies attack resistance directly, users need not verify their identity to complete micro tasks, which circumvents the costs, delays, and privacy surrender attached to centralized identity verification and thereby enlarges the willing labor pool.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "workers staking reputation tokens rather than proving identity"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3128900-046:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "By contrast, on the Semada Platform, users do not need to verify their identity to complete micro tasks. The Semada Protocol architecture, and specifically its reputation token staking mechanism, make the Semada Platform attack resistant.",
      "text_sha256": "738f9e0381878f9f5a4288d573b6cda5f5d338441f11e62c62d96457e6737ed7",
      "source_sha256": "381d72e85d976e2af852e8ec3bba87bc6a05ccb3349a2c3dd6f9e64de96ab4b0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-009",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-009",
      "text": "Users on internet based platforms earn their reputation but do not own it, so if a platform deletes an account, years of reputation data disappear and users have near zero ability to reclaim it.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "ai-and-agents"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "centralized platforms such as Facebook"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-009:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "Users earned their reputation but do NOT own reputation - e.g. if Facebook and other internet-based platform businesses accidentally deleted user account, years of data would be removed and users have near zero ability to reclaim the data",
      "text_sha256": "5307a00adcdcf0ff12361b012ddbc9131fcee6175a7b9a43b6754348eb9c3297",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-017",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-017",
      "text": "Meaningful and secure reputation tokens supply the incentives needed for secure proof of stake consensus in block production, which eliminates the unsustainable inefficiencies of proof of work based blockchains.",
      "claim_type": "design",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation",
        "tokenomics",
        "economics"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "tokens that represent reputation per type of expertise"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 64
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-017:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "giving the proper incentives for guaranteeing secure proof-of- stake consensus protocols for block production. This eliminates the unsustainable inefficiencies of proof-of-work based blockchains.",
      "text_sha256": "7351288eb5717f3e87995cfb3d63cc4bc92db4161ad42cce2fbce6dbad18c22c",
      "source_sha256": "781758dea356e55d79c73ad7f1debe7c83de398bd1cd9e0a9a6c2802f276b4c0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3266953-018",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3266953-018",
      "text": "Semada replaces fungible currency staking with reputation staking for block propagation, a consensus algorithm the authors call Semada Proof of Reputation.",
