    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-036:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The salary payments in fungible stable tokens are in proportion to DevDAO members' respective non-fungible reputation token scores. The indirect economic effects remove corruptive elements and make the governance design more attack resistant and stable in the long run.",
      "text_sha256": "8cf90d036e763066f0c5757b667e3c60da1d6c06b9e443fe031493ee438cc86b",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-038",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-038",
      "text": "DevDAO member reputation is inflationary by design, so that non use, meaning failure to stake reputation tokens or to vote, causes value depreciation, which incentivizes action and makes liveness faults less likely.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "reputation",
        "risk-and-incentives"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 60
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-038:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "The DevDAO member reputation is inflationary in the DevDAO design. As such, non-use, e.g. non-staking of reputation tokens or non-voting, would lead to value depreciation, which incentivizes action and thus value enhancement. Liveness faults become less likely.",
      "text_sha256": "c67784fd122a622b34ee94be18ebb8d14e0e1092a9c9fa0c452805e5c06a2b65",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-039",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3652481-039",
      "text": "Reputation weighted salary distribution defeats sock puppet attacks, because a member who creates ten accounts holding one reputation token each ends up in the same position as one account holding ten reputation tokens.",
      "claim_type": "mechanism",
      "topics": [
        "consensus-and-security",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "salary is distributed in proportion to reputation token holdings"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "argued",
      "relevance_score": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3652481-039:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "This solves the sock- puppet attack because if a DevDAO member creates 10 accounts with 1 reputation token each, it is the same as 1 account with 10 reputation tokens.",
      "text_sha256": "0e473dda768300ce95faaf277ea59ec44422f7cc5a38a35c5cc9ea121e119c9f",
      "source_sha256": "530b3a40c244aeca2eb4c53f4c9b4d6b2962bd6be9f92b4ebe17139c17f4c0e0",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-030",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-030",
      "text": "The strong trust that sustained Maghribi trade, in which embezzlement was rare despite extreme information asymmetry, cannot be explained by a strong centralized government, since the Maghribis could not form a centralized legal or political hierarchy and the official legal channels were slow and unreliable.",
      "claim_type": "empirical",
      "topics": [
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "disclosure",
        "reputation",
        "law-and-legal-systems",
        "compliance"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "Maghribi Jewish traders around 1000 AD under the Fatimid caliphate"
      ],
      "attribution_class": "source_derived",
      "attribution_status": "directly_attributable_to_wulf_a_kaal",
      "verification_status": "current",
      "source_quote_status": "present_in_canonical_claim_record",
      "source_quote_individual_match_status": "not_recomputed_by_pilot",
      "confidence": "evidenced",
      "relevance_score": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-030:source-passage",
      "type": "SourcePassage",
      "text": "In point of fact, the records show that such embezzlement was rare. Instead, a strong sense of trust pervaded. So what mechanism protected the principals from their agents' asymmetric information? The answer was not a strong centralized gov- ernment.",
      "text_sha256": "6081ab1bcb7a2692d2e73da08266e18421cac27f37c52d600425c095fef38762",
      "source_sha256": "74df9cc9a19a098bdacd0424a4174795f6e184f7a31c8ee7541195186701ebd2",
      "locator_status": "exact_quote_without_page_locator"
    },
    {
      "id": "kaal:claim:3782193-031",
      "type": "Claim",
      "canonical_url": "https://wulfkaal.github.io/claims/3782193-031",
      "text": "Honesty would be the wrong strategy for an agent if the contract were anonymous and its resolution did not affect future contracts, because that situation is a single-stage zero-sum game in which stealing all the entrusted wealth is optimal.",
      "claim_type": "failure",
      "topics": [
        "economics",
        "ai-and-agents",
        "corporate-governance",
        "reputation"
      ],
      "scope_conditions": [
        "anonymous contracting",
        "no effect of the outcome on future business"
      ],
